 * Portable syscall wrappers.
 *
 * KLEE's POSIX model was written against x86 syscall numbers.  Architectures
 * such as AArch64 only provide the "*at" flavours of several of those calls
 * (there is no __NR_open, __NR_stat, __NR_lstat, __NR_chmod, __NR_chown,
